    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but it feels like a bit of a cop-out to say it's \"both.\" if you had to look at the data, doesn't the growth argument basically carry more weight since it's the foundational economic effect? like, isn't the inequality part more of a political/social critique rather than a flaw in the economic theory itself?",
